WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.167
Missing value handling.

2
00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:07.067
Real tables have holes, and how you fill them can quietly make or break a model.

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:12.200
Most models refuse to train on missing values, so you must decide.

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.900
And the decision is per column, not global.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.000
If a column is mostly empty, drop the column.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.000
If only a few random rows are missing, you can drop those rows.

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.533
Otherwise, impute: fill with the median, the mean, or a per-group value.

8
00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:29.833
Here is the insight interviewers fish for.

9
00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:34.233
The fact that a value is missing often carries information on its own.

10
00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:37.000
Here is the safer pattern.

11
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.067
Start with a column full of holes.

12
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.400
Fill the holes with the median so the model can train.

13
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.223
But also add a was missing flag, a zero or one column.

14
00:00:46.223 --> 00:00:48.833
That keeps the signal the median erased.

15
00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:53.033
In scikit-learn, one object does both jobs.

16
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.500
We choose the median strategy and turn on add indicator, which appends the flag columns automatically.

17
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.300
We fit on the training data only, then apply the same medians to the test set.

18
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.367
The shape grows, and those extra columns are the missingness flags.

19
00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.367
Look at the Exoplanet Archive.

20
00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:17.233
Mass is missing for most planets found by the transit method, because transits can't weigh planets.

21
00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:22.433
Add the flag, and the model learns that unweighed planets tend to be small and distant.

22
00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:24.097
The F1 score climbs.

23
00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:27.233
Imputing silently had thrown that signal away.

24
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:29.212
Let's recap.

25
00:01:29.212 --> 00:01:32.067
Decide per column whether to drop or impute.

26
00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.567
The median is robust to outliers.

27
00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:37.133
Missingness is often a signal in itself.

28
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:39.202
So add a was missing flag.

29
00:01:39.202 --> 00:01:40.767
Next up: data cleaning.
